-->, not <!-- composition: ${e} -->.`,"file.text-control-value":({kind:e,control:t,object:n,slide:o})=>`Control "${t}" of "${n}" ${Ht(e)} "${o}" is a text control. Its words belong in the .md file as <!-- text: ${n}.${t} -->.`,"file.slide-marker-missing":({kind:e,id:t})=>`The .mdpoint file has ${e} "${t}", but the .md file has no marker for it.`,"file.notes-repeated":({kind:e,id:t})=>`The .md file has more than one notes block for ${e} "${t}".`,"file.text-block-repeated":({kind:e,object:t,slide:n})=>`The .md file has more than one <!-- text: ${t} --> block for ${e} "${n}".`,"file.control-block-repeated":({kind:e,control:t,slide:n})=>`The .md file has more than one <!-- control: ${t} --> block for ${e} "${n}".`,"file.paragraph-id-repeated":({block:e,name:t,id:n})=>`A paragraph in ${e} block "${t}" repeats the id "${n}" of an earlier one. It is read as a new paragraph.`,"file.paragraph-id-misspelled":({block:e,name:t,comment:n})=>`"${n}" in ${e} block "${t}" is read as a note, not a paragraph id. A paragraph id ends the paragraph\u2019s last line, as in <!-- id: k3x9a2 -->. An id starts with a lowercase letter, then has lowercase letters and digits with single hyphens between them.`,"file.control-block-missing":({control:e,composition:t})=>`The .md file has no <!-- control: ${e} --> block for composition "${t}". Its instances show no words by default.`,"file.media-type":({file:e,type:t})=>`Media file "${e}" doesn\u2019t match this ${t} object.`,"file.media-file":({file:e})=>`File "${e}" isn\u2019t an image, a video, an audio file, or a GLB.`,"file.media-required":({type:e})=>`Object type ${e} needs a file.`,"file.model-file-required":()=>"A model needs a GLB file.","file.model-file-type":({file:e})=>`A model\u2019s file must be a GLB, not "${e}".`,"file.web-video-url":({at:e})=>`"${e}" must be a YouTube or Vimeo video URL.`,"file.object-type":()=>'Object type must be one of "text", "table", "image", "video", "audio", "web-video", "shape", "path", "icon", "line", "group", "instance", "chart", "camera", "model", "light", "shadow-catcher", "floor", or "world".',"file.camera-elsewhere":({id:e})=>`A camera\u2019s id must be "camera", not "${e}".`,"file.camera-id-taken":({type:e})=>`Only the camera can have the id "camera", not an object of type ${e}.`,"file.world-elsewhere":({id:e})=>`The World\u2019s id must be "world", not "${e}".`,"file.world-id-taken":({type:e})=>`Only the World can have the id "world", not an object of type ${e}.`,"file.parent-id":()=>'"parent" must be an object\u2019s id.',"file.3d-position":()=>'A model, a light, or a shadow catcher needs "position": { x, y, z }.',"file.floor-parent":()=>"A floor can\u2019t have a parent.","file.floor-position":({at:e})=>`"${e}": a floor moves only up and down, along "y".`,"file.light-type-required":()=>'A light needs "light-type" set to one of "directional", "spot", "point", or "area".',"file.light-key":({key:e,type:t,at:n})=>`"${n?`${n}.`:""}${e}" isn\u2019t a key for ${t} lights.`,"file.object-key":({key:e,type:t,at:n})=>`"${n?`${n}.`:""}${e}" isn\u2019t a key for ${t} objects.`,"file.frame-height-auto-size":({at:e})=>`"${e}" can\u2019t have a height. "auto-size" grows the box\u2019s height to fit the text unless the box has a "text-path".`,"file.frame-width-auto-size":({at:e})=>`"${e}" can\u2019t have a width. "auto-size" grows the box\u2019s width to fit the text unless the box has a "text-path" or a "column-count" of 2 or more.`,"file.frame-point-moved":({parts:e})=>e==="both"?'This change makes "frame.x" and "frame.y" name another point of the box. Add "frame.x" and "frame.y" to the override.':`This change makes "frame.${e}" name another point of the box. Add "frame.${e}" to the override.`,"file.frame-height-table":({at:e})=>`"${e}" can\u2019t have a height. A table\u2019s rows set its height.`,"file.frame-width-table":({at:e})=>`"${e}" can\u2019t have a width. A table\u2019s columns set its width.`,"file.light-intensity":({at:e,type:t})=>`${e?`"${e}": `:""}${e?t==="area"?"an":"a":t==="area"?"An":"A"} ${t} light needs "intensity" in watts.`,"file.3d-parent":()=>'"parent" must be the id of a model or a light.',"file.parent-node-without-parent":()=>'"parent-node" needs "parent". It names a node of the parent.',"file.parent-inverse-without-parent":()=>'"parent-inverse" needs "parent". It kept the object in place when it was parented.',"file.boolean":({at:e})=>`"${e}" must be true or false.`,"file.frontmatter-missing":()=>"The .md file must begin with YAML frontmatter.","file.frontmatter-unclosed":()=>"The .md file\u2019s frontmatter has no closing --- line.","file.frontmatter-fence-spaces":()=>"The .md file\u2019s frontmatter has a --- line that ends in spaces or tabs. Remove them.","file.frontmatter-carriage-returns":()=>"The .md file\u2019s frontmatter has a line that ends in a carriage return alone. Save the file with LF or CRLF line endings.","file.section-heading":({id:e})=>`Section "${e}" needs one heading line under its marker, such as # Name.`,"file.section-heading-comment":({id:e,line:t})=>`Section "${e}" has a comment in its heading line. Remove it from "${t}".`,"file.section-repeated":({id:e})=>`Section "${e}" appears more than once.`,"file.marker-outside-slide":()=>"A text, control, or notes marker isn\u2019t under a slide or composition marker. Move it under the slide or composition it belongs to.","file.slide-outside-section":({id:e})=>`Slide "${e}" comes before the first section; once there are sections, every slide must be in one.`,"file.frontmatter-one-line":({key:e})=>`"${e}" in the .md file\u2019s frontmatter must be on one line.`,"file.frontmatter-twice":({key:e})=>`"${e}" appears more than once in the .md file\u2019s frontmatter.`,"file.frontmatter-escape":({key:e})=>`"${e}" in the .md file\u2019s frontmatter has an invalid YAML escape sequence.`,"file.frontmatter-form":({key:e})=>`"${e}" in the .md file\u2019s frontmatter must be written as "${e}: value".`,"file.frontmatter-plain":({key:e,quoted:t})=>`"${e}" needs its value in quotes, as in ${t}.`,"file.json-root":({file:e})=>`${e} must be one record.`,"file.format-version":({at:e,readable:t})=>`"${e}" must be a version in quotes, such as "${t}".`,"file.newer-minor-kept":()=>"This presentation uses features from a newer MarkdownPoint. They\u2019re kept as they are.","file.rounded-number":()=>"Some numbers in this presentation have more than six decimal places. MarkdownPoint rounds them to six.","file.issue-count-limit":({count:e})=>`MarkdownPoint leaves out ${e===1?"1 more issue":`${Le(e)} more issues`}.`,"file.uuid":({at:e})=>`"${e}" must be a lowercase UUID.`,"file.theme-key":({at:e})=>`"${e}" must be a theme key: a folder name in the presentation\u2019s themes folder, such as "basic".`,"file.scheme-name":({at:e})=>`"${e}" must be a scheme name.`,"file.file-path":({at:e})=>`"${e}" must be a file path in the presentation\u2019s or the theme\u2019s folder.`,"file.marker-id":({marker:e,id:t})=>`Invalid ${e} marker id "${t}".`,"file.marker-line-break":({marker:e})=>`The ${e} marker must end with a line break.`,"file.marker-unsupported":({line:e})=>`Unsupported marker "${e}": the .md file uses only <!-- section: id -->, <!-- slide: id -->, <!-- composition: id -->, <!-- text: id -->, <!-- control: id -->, and <!-- notes -->. None of them has a closing marker.`,"file.marker-invalid":({line:e})=>`Malformed MarkdownPoint marker "${e}".`,"file.code-block-unclosed":()=>"A code block isn\u2019t closed. Every marker after it is read as code.","file.merge-conflict":()=>"A merge conflict starts here. Keep the lines you want and delete the <<<<<<<, =======, and >>>>>>> lines.","file.words-before-slide":()=>"Text before the first slide marker belongs to no slide; put it under a slide\u2019s text or notes marker.","file.words-outside-slide":()=>"Text outside a slide block belongs to no slide; put it under a slide\u2019s text or notes marker.","file.words-outside-blocks":({kind:e,id:t})=>e==="slide"?`Slide "${t}" has text outside its text